{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come in, Mr. Alvarez. Coffee in the lounge is burnt, don't bother. What's the trouble?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Blocked nose.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Both sides? Where's the pressure?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Both. Cheeks.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): What color is the discharge, is it thick, and how many days for the blocked nose, the cheek pressure, and the discharge?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Green. Thick. Ten days.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): A cold before this, and is that cold gone now?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Gone.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): When did the cold start?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. Last winter, or the one before.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Err, last winter or the one before doesn't line up with ten days at all. Can you date this cold?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Can't.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok then, I'm not gonna force a date. You tired with this?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Second week.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever, cough, or shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Allergies to medicines, penicillin or anything else?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): You using a nasal spray?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Afrin. Daily. Two each side.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Other medicines you take?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Amlodipine for the pressure, five milligrams, mornings, by mouth.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. So the pressure, your blood pressure. What else?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): The cholesterol one at night, twenty milligrams. Don't know the name.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): And sugar?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Sugar tablets, five hundred milligrams, twice a day. Don't remember.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Herbal, or something from the shop?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Only the Ayurvedic powder in the morning. A spoon.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): The azithromicin z-pack, still taking it?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Stopped it in March.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Did you ever take the Flonase?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Alright. Temp is 98.2, uh, blood pressure one thirty six over 82, heart rate 78, oxygen 98 percent. Nose lining looks swollen on both sides, thick green mucus on the right, cheeks are tender, throat is clear, lungs are clear.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me think out loud, ten days of green stuff and tender cheeks with no fever reads as acute rhinosinusitis, probably viral, though I can't fully rule out a bacterial sinus infection. Most of these settle without antibiotics, so none today. Stop the Afrin, daily use rebounds and keeps the nose blocked. Saline rinses a couple times a day.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Ok.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Back-up if you need it. If you're not better in seven days or you get a fever, start amoxicillin five hundred milligrams three times a day for seven days. If it isn't settling by next week, come back in. If an eye swells or vision changes, go to the ER."
 ],
